=== LAS benchmark  (mode 3, 2000 iters/op) ===
params: n=4  ell=4  kappa=60  gamma=122880  N=256  Q=8380417

  Setup          28.16 us
  KeyGen         34.60 us   [statement gen = same cost]
  Sign          320.37 us
  Verify         78.41 us
  PreSign       357.84 us
  PreVerify      84.04 us
  Adapt          87.64 us
  Ext            28.12 us

Rejection-sampling (MEASURED directly via las_attempts, 2000 sigs):
  Sign    : 2.675 attempts/sig  -> acceptance 37.4%, retries 1.675
  PreSign : 2.817 attempts/sig  -> acceptance 35.5%, retries 1.817
  Theory  : (1 - k/g)^(M*N) = 36.8% per attempt (~2.72 attempts)
  Rejection sampling is intrinsic to Fiat-Shamir-with-aborts (optimised
  Dilithium also rejects, targeting a small expected repeat count); this
  simplified scheme just omits the hint vector, keeping the algebra clear.

--- Object sizes ---
  In-memory (sizeof, full int32 per coeff):
    pk / statement Y : 4096 bytes
    sk / witness y   : 8192 bytes
    sig / pre-sig    : 9216 bytes

  Theoretical packed (formula, this implementation's params):
    pk / statement Y : 2944 bytes  [LAS_N*N*ceil(log2(Q)) bits; Q=8380417 => 23 bits/coeff]
    sk / witness y   :  512 bytes  [LAS_M*N*2 bits; ternary needs 2 bits/coeff]
    sig / pre-sig    : 4676 bytes  [c: 68 bytes; z: 18 bits/coeff => 4608 bytes]

  Paper's estimate (~3210 bytes for signature):
    Refers to the paper's OPTIMISED scheme (q~2^24, n=4, ell=4,
    bit-packed with hint vector). Not directly comparable to this
    implementation which uses q~2^23, no hints, and is unoptimised.
    The correct comparison point is our 'theoretical packed' column above.

Correctness: 100% over 2000 Sign/Verify and 2000 PreSign/PreVerify iters
